INFO  [Claude Code] The error message indicated: "Diffblue Cover was unable to construct an instance of Specification. No suitable constructor or factory method found."
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Root Cause
INFO  [Claude Code] `Specification` is an interface from Spring Data JPA that cannot be instantiated directly. Diffblue Cover needs concrete factory methods or constructors to create test instances.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Solution Implemented
INFO  [Claude Code] Created a helper class `SpecificationHelper.java` in `/home/jbergqvist/diffblue/mawensen-erp/src/test/java/com/yufeng/util/SpecificationHelper.java` with static factory methods that provide testable Specification instances:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Factory Methods Provided:**
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. `matchAll()` - Returns a specification that matches all entities (conjunction predicate)
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. `matchNone()` - Returns a specification that matches no entities (disjunction predicate)
INFO  [Claude Code] 3. `equalTo(fieldName, value)` - Filters by field equality
INFO  [Claude Code] 4. `like(fieldName, pattern)` - Filters by LIKE pattern on string fields
INFO  [Claude Code] 5. `notEqualTo(fieldName, value)` - Filters by field inequality
INFO  [Claude Code] 6. `and(spec1, spec2)` - Combines two specifications with AND logic
INFO  [Claude Code] 7. `or(spec1, spec2)` - Combines two specifications with OR logic
INFO  [Claude Code] 8. `nullSafe(spec)` - Provides null-safe wrapper for specifications
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### How This Addresses R083 Errors
INFO  [Claude Code] Diffblue Cover will now be able to:
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. Import and use these factory methods in generated tests
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. Create concrete Specification instances for testing repository methods
INFO  [Claude Code] 3. Test various query scenarios (all, none, filtered, combined predicates)
INFO  [Claude Code] 4. Generate comprehensive test coverage for methods that previously failed with R083 errors
INFO  [Claude Code] 
